# `role <name>` with its `take` globs, and any `mark` flags that change how the
# files it matches are READ rather than which mill reads them. `mark lean` is the
# only one today: see note/term/lean.md.
#
# ONE LIST HOLDING BOTH, so a `mark` may be written above or below the `take`
# lines. Two separate `mine list`s would fix the order, and there is no reason a
# reader should have to remember one.
#
# A LOCAL `role-mark` rather than a load of `@term/mill/tree/code/mark/mine`: that
# rule carries `bind key, value` children a role has no use for, and the deck
# grammar bundle is generated from `deck/mill/code/tree/deck` alone, so reaching across
# roles would widen what the bundler has to follow for no gain.
mine role
  mine term, term role
    mine term
      site name
    mine list
      mine any
        mine form, like role-mark
          site mark
        mine form, like role-take
          site take

mine role-mark
  mine term, term mark
    mine term
      site name

mine role-take
  mine term, term take
    mine path
      site glob
    mine list
      mine form, like role-miss
        site miss

mine role-miss
  mine term, term miss
    mine path
      site glob
